        "comments": "The assembly drRosRubi1.hap1.1 is based on 51x PacBio data and Arima2 Hi-C data generated by the Darwin Tree of Life Project\n(https://www.darwintreeoflife.org/). The assembly process included the following sequence of steps: initial PacBio assembly generation with Hifiasm in Hi-C integrated assembly mode, and Hi-C based scaffolding with YaHS. The mitochondrial and plastid genomes were assembled using OATK. Finally, each haplotype assembly was analysed and manually improved using TreeVal. Chromosome-scale scaffolds confirmed by the Hi-C data have been named in order of size. Sample is pentaploid (5n=35) and has unusual asymetric meiosis called 'canina meiosis' where 7 pairs of chromosomes recombine and the remaining 21 are inherited as univalents through the egg cell. Recombining pairs of chromosomes were identified based on sequence similarity (inferred from the HIC contact map). One set of 7 putatively recombining chromosomes was placed in the HAP1 assembly alongside the 21 univalents. The other set of 7 putatively recombining chromosomes have been placed in the HAP2 assembly. Recombining chromosomes are named 1 to 7 in size order with the remaining univalent chromosomeos named 8 - 28 in size order. The order and orientation of the scaffolds making up the following scaffolds are uncertain: HAP1 - Chromosome 5 from 22.31 to 23.49, Chromosome 7 from 5.97 to 11.83 and on HAP2 - Chromosome 7 from 6.11 to 12.24 Mbp.",
